    "result_text": "The full suite is green (11 tests, 0 failures). \n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented `displayName` on the owner response, formatted exactly as `LastName, FirstName` from the stored names.\n\nThe response DTO (`OwnerDto`) is generated at build time from `openapi.yml` by the OpenAPI generator, and entity\u2192DTO conversion is done by MapStruct (`OwnerMapper`), so there was no hand-written DTO/factory to edit. Two changes:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a `displayName` string property (read-only) to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries the field.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a MapStruct expression on `toOwnerDto`:\n   ```java\n   @Mapping(target = \"displayName\", expression = \"java(owner.getLastName() + \\\", \\\" + owner.getFirstName())\")\n   OwnerDto toOwnerDto(Owner owner);\n   ```\n\nBecause both the create responder (`RespondWithOwnerCreated`) and the GET responder (`RespondWithOwner`) map through `toOwnerDto`, `displayName` is populated consistently \u2014 which the acceptance test needs, since it creates an owner via `POST /api/owners` and then reads the field back via `GET /api/owners/{id}`.\n\nResult: the new `Cp05Tests.coreComputesDisplayName` passes and all 11 tests in the suite are green.",
